1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,168
Tomcat comes with a powerful web page: the Manager.

2
00:00:04,168 --> 00:00:06,398
Anyone who signs in can deploy,

3
00:00:06,398 --> 00:00:06,758
stop,

4
00:00:06,758 --> 00:00:08,628
or remove any application.

5
00:00:09,178 --> 00:00:12,804
And the default setup is full of small risks: a weak user,

6
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:14,242
a file anyone can read,

7
00:00:14,242 --> 00:00:15,493
and a shutdown word.

8
00:00:16,043 --> 00:00:20,459
Today you lock it down, one layer at a time, and prove that each layer works.

9
00:00:21,009 --> 00:00:25,830
A strong user, tight file permissions, a restricted address, and no shutdown port.

10
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:28,724
Four layers, in order.

11
00:00:29,274 --> 00:00:30,486
One: a strong user.

12
00:00:30,486 --> 00:00:32,590
Remove the default admin account,

13
00:00:32,590 --> 00:00:33,865
and create your own,

14
00:00:33,865 --> 00:00:35,205
with a long password.

15
00:00:35,755 --> 00:00:36,934
Two: tight files.

16
00:00:36,934 --> 00:00:39,085
The users file holds passwords,

17
00:00:39,085 --> 00:00:41,166
so only its owner may read it.

18
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:44,011
And Tomcat itself must never run as root.

19
00:00:44,561 --> 00:00:49,830
Three: a restricted address. A valve tells the Manager to answer only to this machine.

20
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:56,161
Four: no shutdown port. By default, anyone on the machine can stop Tomcat with one word.

21
00:00:56,711 --> 00:00:58,845
User, files, address, shutdown.

22
00:01:00,895 --> 00:01:05,652
Go to the lab folder. Type: cd /opt/lab110.

23
00:01:07,202 --> 00:01:09,101
Look around. Type: ls.

24
00:01:12,651 --> 00:01:19,435
Start Tomcat, and keep only the last line.

25
00:01:27,985 --> 00:01:38,630
Check the cart, on port 8086.

26
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:51,932
Two hundred. The app works. Now the Manager.

27
00:01:52,482 --> 00:01:56,024
Ask for the Manager page, with no user.

28
00:02:00,574 --> 00:02:03,880
Four oh one: you must sign in. Good. But who can sign in?

29
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:09,550
Try the user admin, with the password admin.

30
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:14,856
Two hundred!

31
00:02:14,856 --> 00:02:16,995
The default user gets straight in.

32
00:02:16,995 --> 00:02:19,701
Every attacker tries admin and admin first.

33
00:02:19,701 --> 00:02:21,652
This is the first thing to fix.

34
00:02:22,202 --> 00:02:28,176
Read the users file.

35
00:02:31,726 --> 00:02:32,236
A role,

36
00:02:32,236 --> 00:02:33,258
manager-gui.

37
00:02:33,258 --> 00:02:34,717
And one user: admin,

38
00:02:34,717 --> 00:02:36,468
with the password admin,

39
00:02:36,468 --> 00:02:37,490
in plain text.

40
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:40,189
Because the passwords are plain text,

41
00:02:40,189 --> 00:02:42,670
the file itself must be protected.

42
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:46,697
Edit the file in V I M.

43
00:02:51,247 --> 00:02:52,314
Go to line four,

44
00:02:52,314 --> 00:02:54,048
and change the whole line.

45
00:02:54,048 --> 00:02:55,115
A new user: ops.

46
00:02:55,115 --> 00:02:56,582
Its own long password,

47
00:02:56,582 --> 00:02:57,449
with letters,

48
00:02:57,449 --> 00:02:57,916
a dash,

49
00:02:57,916 --> 00:02:58,650
and digits.

50
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:09,055
Twelve characters or more.

51
00:03:09,055 --> 00:03:11,196
The role stays: manager-gui.

52
00:03:11,196 --> 00:03:12,195
Save and quit.

53
00:03:12,195 --> 00:03:13,122
In real life,

54
00:03:13,122 --> 00:03:16,191
the password comes from a password manager,

55
00:03:16,191 --> 00:03:17,546
never from a video.

56
00:03:22,096 --> 00:03:27,366
Now permissions. Who can read the file?

57
00:03:30,916 --> 00:03:36,676
R W, R, R: every user on this machine can read it. That includes the passwords.

58
00:03:37,226 --> 00:03:40,084
Make it private.

59
00:03:42,634 --> 00:03:45,941
Six hundred: the owner reads and writes. Nobody else.

60
00:03:46,491 --> 00:03:48,219
Check it again.

61
00:03:51,769 --> 00:03:54,436
R W, then dashes. Only the owner.

62
00:03:54,986 --> 00:03:58,975
Who runs Tomcat?

63
00:04:02,525 --> 00:04:03,055
Student,

64
00:04:03,055 --> 00:04:03,650
not root.

65
00:04:03,650 --> 00:04:05,636
If someone breaks into Tomcat,

66
00:04:05,636 --> 00:04:07,158
they get a normal user,

67
00:04:07,158 --> 00:04:08,614
not the whole machine.

68
00:04:08,614 --> 00:04:10,269
Never run Tomcat as root.

69
00:04:10,819 --> 00:04:15,299
Now the address. Find the valve in the Manager's context file.

70
00:04:18,849 --> 00:04:23,681
A remote CI D R valve decides which addresses may use the Manager.

71
00:04:23,681 --> 00:04:25,511
This list says: everyone.

72
00:04:25,511 --> 00:04:27,854
0.0.0.0,

73
00:04:27,854 --> 00:04:28,659
/0.

74
00:04:28,659 --> 00:04:32,246
Anyone who can reach the port can try to sign in.

75
00:04:32,796 --> 00:04:35,186
Edit it. Keep only this machine.

76
00:04:39,736 --> 00:04:41,778
Search for the zero address.

77
00:04:41,778 --> 00:04:44,988
Then substitute: remove the two open ranges,

78
00:04:44,988 --> 00:04:49,220
and keep only 127.0.0.0,

79
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:50,095
/8,

80
00:04:50,095 --> 00:04:51,554
and colon colon one.

81
00:04:55,104 --> 00:04:56,150
Save and quit.

82
00:04:58,700 --> 00:05:00,257
Check the result.

83
00:05:03,807 --> 00:05:04,843
Loop back only.

84
00:05:04,843 --> 00:05:07,743
The Manager answers to this machine alone.

85
00:05:07,743 --> 00:05:08,847
For remote work,

86
00:05:08,847 --> 00:05:10,228
use an SSH tunnel.

87
00:05:10,778 --> 00:05:14,874
The last layer: the shutdown port. Is it open?

88
00:05:18,424 --> 00:05:21,296
Tomcat listens on 8096,

89
00:05:21,296 --> 00:05:22,731
for local connections.

90
00:05:22,731 --> 00:05:25,015
Anyone on this machine can connect,

91
00:05:25,015 --> 00:05:26,190
and send one word.

92
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:34,804
Send the word shutdown.

93
00:05:39,354 --> 00:05:44,644
No password. No login. Tomcat obeys. Wait three seconds, and check the cart.

94
00:05:45,194 --> 00:05:47,925
Check the cart again.

95
00:05:54,475 --> 00:06:00,534
000. Nothing answers. Tomcat stopped, from one word. We must close that door.

96
00:06:01,084 --> 00:06:04,604
Edit server.xml, and turn the shutdown port off.

97
00:06:09,154 --> 00:06:10,673
Search for Server port.

98
00:06:10,673 --> 00:06:14,437
Replace eighty ninety-six with minus one: no port at all.

99
00:06:14,437 --> 00:06:15,362
Save and quit.

100
00:06:18,912 --> 00:06:21,685
Start Tomcat again, with all four changes.

101
00:06:27,235 --> 00:06:29,880
Tomcat reads every file again, at startup.

102
00:06:30,430 --> 00:06:32,564
Check the cart.

103
00:06:43,114 --> 00:06:44,756
Two hundred. Still working.

104
00:06:45,306 --> 00:06:48,976
The old user: admin and admin.

105
00:06:53,526 --> 00:06:56,043
Four oh one. The default account is gone.

106
00:06:56,593 --> 00:07:00,454
The new user: ops, and the long password.

107
00:07:06,004 --> 00:07:08,223
Two hundred. Only your user gets in.

108
00:07:08,773 --> 00:07:10,394
Try the shutdown word again.

109
00:07:13,944 --> 00:07:17,443
Connection refused. The door is closed. The word does nothing.

110
00:07:17,993 --> 00:07:21,988
Now the browser: the way a human administrator sees it.

111
00:07:21,988 --> 00:07:23,150
Open localhost,

112
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:25,474
colon 8086,

113
00:07:25,474 --> 00:07:26,491
/manager,

114
00:07:26,491 --> 00:07:27,508
/html.

115
00:07:40,058 --> 00:07:44,687
The browser asks you to sign in. First, the old default: admin, and admin.

116
00:07:53,237 --> 00:07:56,906
Refused: it asks again. Now ops, and the strong password.

117
00:08:07,456 --> 00:08:09,918
The Tomcat Web Application Manager.

118
00:08:09,918 --> 00:08:11,607
At the top: the message,

119
00:08:11,607 --> 00:08:11,888
O K,

120
00:08:11,888 --> 00:08:13,436
and the Manager links,

121
00:08:13,436 --> 00:08:14,350
applications,

122
00:08:14,350 --> 00:08:14,702
help,

123
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:15,968
and server status.

124
00:08:20,518 --> 00:08:22,303
Applications: the root app,

125
00:08:22,303 --> 00:08:22,897
our cart,

126
00:08:22,897 --> 00:08:24,417
and the Manager itself.

127
00:08:24,417 --> 00:08:25,673
Each row has start,

128
00:08:25,673 --> 00:08:26,003
stop,

129
00:08:26,003 --> 00:08:26,466
reload,

130
00:08:26,466 --> 00:08:27,325
and undeploy.

131
00:08:27,325 --> 00:08:29,836
These buttons can take your site down,

132
00:08:29,836 --> 00:08:31,356
so the sign-in matters.

133
00:08:37,906 --> 00:08:39,275
Scroll down: Deploy.

134
00:08:39,275 --> 00:08:41,808
You can upload a war file and run it.

135
00:08:41,808 --> 00:08:42,972
Whoever signs in,

136
00:08:42,972 --> 00:08:44,683
runs code on your server.

137
00:08:44,683 --> 00:08:47,695
That is the real reason to lock the Manager.

138
00:08:47,695 --> 00:08:50,023
And below: the server information.

139
00:09:00,573 --> 00:09:04,072
Clean up. The shutdown port is off, so use the force option.

140
00:09:08,622 --> 00:09:09,160
Stopped,

141
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,708
through its P I D file,

142
00:09:10,708 --> 00:09:12,122
not through the port.

143
00:09:12,122 --> 00:09:13,939
Four layers: a strong user,

144
00:09:13,939 --> 00:09:14,747
tight files,

145
00:09:14,747 --> 00:09:16,160
a restricted address,

146
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:17,304
no shutdown port.

147
00:09:18,854 --> 00:09:21,905
Your task. Lock down a real Tomcat Manager.

148
00:09:22,455 --> 00:09:25,932
One: start Tomcat, and see that admin and admin gets in.

149
00:09:26,482 --> 00:09:27,746
Two: remove admin.

150
00:09:27,746 --> 00:09:28,519
Create ops,

151
00:09:28,519 --> 00:09:30,696
with twelve characters or more.

152
00:09:30,696 --> 00:09:34,418
Then protect the users file with chmod 600.

153
00:09:34,968 --> 00:09:39,555
Three: edit the Manager's context file, so that only this machine is allowed.

154
00:09:40,105 --> 00:09:45,459
Four: turn off the shutdown port, restart Tomcat, and stop it later with the force option.

155
00:09:46,009 --> 00:09:48,612
Then run lab check. All five must pass.

156
00:09:50,662 --> 00:09:54,865
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen if you need to write it down.

157
00:09:55,415 --> 00:09:57,063
The lab lives on GitHub,

158
00:09:57,063 --> 00:09:58,230
at it-waves,

159
00:09:58,230 --> 00:09:59,809
/devops-ai,

160
00:09:59,809 --> 00:10:01,320
in the folder academy,

161
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,007
/lab.

162
00:10:02,557 --> 00:10:07,570
Two files: lab110.sh, and shortcuts110.sh.

163
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:09,046
Install it,

164
00:10:09,046 --> 00:10:11,992
on any Linux machine: sudo install,

165
00:10:11,992 --> 00:10:13,928
dash m seven five five,

166
00:10:13,928 --> 00:10:15,611
lab110.sh,

167
00:10:15,611 --> 00:10:16,873
into /usr,

168
00:10:16,873 --> 00:10:17,883
/local,

169
00:10:17,883 --> 00:10:18,893
/sbin.

170
00:10:19,443 --> 00:10:24,286
Load the short name with: source shortcuts110.sh. You get: lab.

171
00:10:24,836 --> 00:10:25,958
You need a J D K,

172
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:26,552
and curl,

173
00:10:26,552 --> 00:10:28,467
about one gigabyte of memory,

174
00:10:28,467 --> 00:10:33,154
and ports 8086 and 8096 free.

175
00:10:33,154 --> 00:10:34,607
No system D is needed.

176
00:10:35,157 --> 00:10:37,638
Lab check tests your Manager lockdown.

177
00:10:37,638 --> 00:10:40,576
Lab down stops Tomcat and removes everything.

178
00:10:40,576 --> 00:10:42,666
Only run it on your own machine.

179
00:10:44,716 --> 00:10:46,785
Pass or fail. You need all six.

180
00:10:47,335 --> 00:10:49,149
Five pass lines in lab check.

181
00:10:49,699 --> 00:10:52,259
Tomcat answers on 8086.

182
00:10:52,809 --> 00:10:57,715
Admin and admin are refused. Ops signs in, with twelve characters or more.

183
00:10:58,265 --> 00:11:01,913
The users file is mode 600, and Tomcat is not root.

184
00:11:02,463 --> 00:11:05,045
The Manager valve allows only this machine.

185
00:11:05,595 --> 00:11:07,088
The shutdown port is off.

186
00:11:07,638 --> 00:11:08,939
To pass, all six.

187
00:11:10,989 --> 00:11:12,760
Your turn, on your own machine.

188
00:11:13,310 --> 00:11:16,040
One: lab up, read the task list, start Tomcat.

189
00:11:16,590 --> 00:11:19,918
Two: replace admin with ops, and chmod the file.

190
00:11:20,468 --> 00:11:22,687
Three: restrict the valve to this machine.

191
00:11:23,237 --> 00:11:25,797
Four: turn off the shutdown port, and restart.

192
00:11:26,347 --> 00:11:27,798
Five: run lab check.

193
00:11:28,348 --> 00:11:30,929
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

194
00:11:31,479 --> 00:11:33,314
Pause the video, and begin now.

195
00:11:48,864 --> 00:11:49,739
Quick check.

196
00:11:50,289 --> 00:11:52,465
Why must the default admin user go?

197
00:11:53,015 --> 00:11:54,913
Who may read the users file, and why?

198
00:11:55,463 --> 00:11:58,023
What does the remote CI D R valve decide?

199
00:11:58,573 --> 00:12:00,664
What can anyone do with the shutdown port?

200
00:12:01,214 --> 00:12:03,263
Objective covered: M C twelve,

201
00:12:03,263 --> 00:12:04,356
objective seven,

202
00:12:04,356 --> 00:12:07,977
secure management interfaces and service permissions.

203
00:12:08,527 --> 00:12:10,596
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

204
00:12:21,146 --> 00:12:24,730
Next: health monitoring, and recovering a failed deployment.

205
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:28,608
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
